---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import PageHeader from "../components/common/PageHeader.astro";
import CTA from "../components/common/CTA.astro";
const BASE = import.meta.env.BASE_URL || "/";
---

<BaseLayout title="About">
    <section id="content" class="s-content">
        <PageHeader pretitle="About Me" title="Hi, I’m Ethan" />

        <section class="s-pagecontent pagecontent">
            <div class="row pageintro">
                <div class="column xl-6 lg-12">
                    <h2 class="text-display-title">
                        Building smarter strategies with data and insight
                    </h2>
                </div>
                <div class="column xl-6 lg-12 u-flexitem-x-right">
                    <p class="lead">
                        If there’s a common thread in my work, it’s a
                        fascination with how systems function and how deliberate
                        design can improve functional efficiency. I’m drawn to
                        the mechanics of decision-making: how people, data, and
                        structure converge to produce outcomes. Whether through
                        analytics, strategy, or innovation, I’m motivated by the
                        pursuit of clarity, translating complexity into order
                        and ideas into impact.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>
            <!-- end pageintro -->

            <div class="row pagemedia">
                <d class="column xl-12">
                    <figure class="page-media">
                        <img
                            src="images/thumbs/about/about-1200.jpg"
                            srcset="images/thumbs/about/about-2400.jpg 2400w, 
                                             images/thumbs/about/about-1200.jpg 1200w, 
                                             images/thumbs/about/about-600.jpg 600w"
                            sizes="(max-width: 2400px) 100vw, 2400px"
                            alt=""
                        />
                    </figure>
                </d>
            </div>
            <!-- end pagemedia -->

            <div class="row width-narrower pagemain">
                <div class="column xl-12">
                    <h2>How I Got Here</h2>
                    <p>
                        My journey began at Woodside High School, where I served
                        as ASB President and developed an early appreciation for
                        how institutions operate—and how they can evolve through
                        thoughtful leadership. Guiding a team through the
                        turbulence of COVID-19 and modernizing the student
                        government’s framework revealed a simple truth: systems,
                        no matter how well-intentioned, depend on design. That
                        experience sparked a lasting fascination with how
                        structure, incentives, and collaboration shape
                        performance.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        At the University of California, San Diego, I pursued
                        that curiosity through a B.S. in Management Science—a
                        discipline rooted in economics and optimization theory
                        that bridges systems thinking with analytical rigor. I
                        paired it with a minor in Data Science to deepen my
                        technical and empirical fluency, combining quantitative
                        reasoning with computational insight.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        That mindset carried into my professional life. Each
                        environment—whether analytical, strategic, or
                        entrepreneurial—reinforced my belief that enduring
                        progress comes from structure built with purpose. Today,
                        I see my career as part of a broader continuum:
                        connecting technical precision with strategic foresight
                        to help organizations become smarter, faster, and more
                        adaptable.
                    </p>

                    <h2 class="u-add-bottom">My Values & Beliefs</h2>

                    <div class="grid-list-items list-items">
                        <div
                            class="grid-list-items__item list-items__item u-remove-bottom"
                        >
                            <div class="list-items__item-header">
                                <h6 class="list-items__item-small-title">
                                    Structure Enables Freedom
                                </h6>
                            </div>
                            <p>
                                Structure doesn’t restrict creativity—it enables
                                it. Clear systems and defined roles allow people
                                to take ownership and operate at their best.
                                Whether leading a team, designing workflows, or
                                developing strategies, I’ve found that good
                                organization creates the space for autonomy,
                                accountability, and innovation to thrive.
                            </p>
                        </div>
                        <div
                            class="grid-list-items__item list-items__item u-remove-bottom"
                        >
                            <div class="list-items__item-header">
                                <h6 class="list-items__item-small-title">
                                    Efficiency as a Form of Respect
                                </h6>
                            </div>
                            <p>
                                Efficiency isn’t about speed—it’s about
                                intention. Doing things well the first time,
                                valuing people’s time, and aligning effort with
                                impact are forms of respect. I’ve learned that
                                the best work happens when the cost-to-value
                                ratio improves for everyone involved—when time
                                and energy are invested where they matter most.
                            </p>
                        </div>
                        <div
                            class="grid-list-items__item list-items__item u-remove-bottom"
                        >
                            <div class="list-items__item-header">
                                <h6 class="list-items__item-small-title">
                                    Curiosity Without Constraint
                                </h6>
                            </div>
                            <p>
                                Every idea starts as a “stupid idea” until it
                                works. I value environments where people can
                                think aloud, experiment freely, and be wrong
                                without penalty. Many of the most meaningful
                                insights I’ve found—whether in data, design, or
                                leadership—emerged from questions that initially
                                seemed naïve. Curiosity, when paired with
                                discipline, is the spark that keeps systems
                                evolving.
                            </p>
                        </div>
                        <div
                            class="grid-list-items__item list-items__item u-remove-bottom"
                        >
                            <div class="list-items__item-header">
                                <h6 class="list-items__item-small-title">
                                    Context Before Conclusion
                                </h6>
                            </div>
                            <p>
                                No problem exists in isolation. I believe
                                effective decision-making begins with
                                understanding the system around the issue—the
                                incentives, dependencies, and trade-offs that
                                define it. Whether in analytics, venture, or
                                leadership, I’ve learned that clarity comes not
                                from immediate answers, but from asking the
                                right questions and seeing the full picture
                                before acting.
                            </p>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <!--grid-list-items -->

                    <h2>What I Bring to the Table</h2>
                    <p>
                        I bring cross-functional experience across venture
                        capital, data analytics, strategic consulting, and
                        startup development. Over the past several years, I’ve
                        supported fund design and thesis development at an
                        early-stage VC, built machine-learning models for a
                        database with over one million records for UC San Diego,
                        and contributed to market strategy and product
                        validation for emerging-tech firms. My background blends
                        economic reasoning with technical fluency in Python,
                        SQL, R, and Excel, alongside practical skills in data
                        visualization, modeling, and business strategy.
                    </p>
                </div>
                <!-- end grid-block-->
            </div>
            <!-- end pagemain -->
        </section>
        <!-- pagecontent -->

        <section class="s-testimonials">
            <div class="row width-narrower pagemain">
                <div class="column xl-12">
                    <h2>Beyond the Résumé</h2>
                    <p>
                        Before I ever studied systems or strategy, I was
                        fascinated by rhythm. I’ve been a lifelong classical and
                        jazz pianist for nearly two decades—my first discipline
                        and the foundation of how I learned to balance structure
                        with creativity. That pursuit led naturally into other
                        forms of expression: performing in musical theatre,
                        exploring photography and video editing, and eventually,
                        dance.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        In college, that creative thread evolved into a deep
                        commitment to salsa and bachata. I’ve had the privilege
                        of training under world champions Liz Rojas and John
                        Narvaez, and later with the legendary Terry Alianza and
                        Cécile Ovide, experiences that deepened my respect for
                        both artistry and discipline. Dance became a space where
                        rhythm met intuition and precision met connection. It is
                        a lifelong passion and hobby of mine that I endeavor to
                        share with the world.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        Outside of the arts, that same attention to detail finds
                        other outlets. I once raced motorcycles, drawn to the
                        balance of precision and control that mirrors my
                        fascination with iteration and efficiency. And when I’m
                        not creating or building, I gravitate toward strategy
                        games and puzzles—systems that reward foresight,
                        adaptability, and elegant solutions.
                    </p>
                </div>
                <!-- end grid-block-->
            </div>
            <!-- end pagemain -->
        </section>

        <section id="cta" class="s-cta">
            <CTA BASE={BASE} />
        </section>
    </section>
</BaseLayout>
